        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(skills): capture reusable techniques from successful work",
        "body": "Closes #105672\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpt-in Skill Workshop autonomy can capture explicit corrections, but reusable procedures discovered during long successful work are otherwise lost when the user did not phrase the result as a correction.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWhen autonomous capture is enabled, successful foreground turns with at least ten model iterations may schedule a separate learning review after the run has finished and the whole agent system has remained idle for 30 seconds. The delayed review rechecks live autonomy, sandbox, agent, provider, sender, and conversation tool policy before it starts.\n\nThe reviewer is isolated to the exact resolved provider and model, reuses the auth profile when available, and disables model fallback. It runs on a dedicated background lane and receives a bounded rendering of only the current turn. Its Skill Workshop surface permits list/inspect plus at most one create or revise mutation; live-skill updates and proposal lifecycle actions are unavailable. Every generated result remains a pending proposal for human review.\n\nThe evidence bar is intentionally narrow: concrete struggle, correction, repeated failure, or a stable procedure expected to save at least two future model/tool round trips. Routine success, one-off facts, preferences, transient failures, secrets, generic advice, and uncertain cases must abstain.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers who explicitly enable autonomous Skill Workshop capture can receive reviewable learning proposals after meaningful work without delaying foreground requests. The feature remains off by default, waits for idle state across embedded and reply-backed runs, bounds retained work, serializes learning reviews, and never applies a proposal automatically.\n\nThe new Self-learning guide documents enablement, eligibility, transcript and provider behavior, cost and privacy implications, proposal-only permissions, review commands, and troubleshooting. Skill Workshop, skills configuration, navigation, and the generated docs map link to that guide.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox [run 29221332451](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29221332451): 32 focused scheduler, Workshop, and lane tests passed; Oxlint reported zero findings; `tsgo:core` and `tsgo:core:test` passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox [run 29222289445](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29222289445): final scheduler suite passed after exact-model fail-closed pinning; Oxlint and both TypeScript lanes passed.\n- Public-network AWS Crabbox run `run_07545709b518`: live OpenAI evaluation created exactly one pending proposal for a recovered deployment preflight and created no additional proposal for a routine one-off audit.\n- Docs validation: `docs:check-mdx`, `docs:check-links`, `docs:check-i18n-glossary`, `docs:map:check`, `format:docs:check`, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
